  "id": "DrugBank_DB13257 - MONDO_1239",
  "verbalization": "Ferrous Sulfate Anhydrous is implicated in the pathogenesis of Anemia of Prematurity through a series of mechanistic links. The evidence suggests that it is used in the treatment of Iron Deficiency Anemia, which in turn is associated with Microcytic Anemia, both of which are linked to Anemia of Prematurity. This indicates a potential role of Ferrous Sulfate Anhydrous in the management of anemia in preterm infants, possibly by correcting iron deficiency and improving red blood cell morphology. The observed indications suggest that the drug may be repurposed for this condition, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence is supported by a consistent pathway across multiple paths, highlighting a potential clinical utility in the treatment of Anemia of Prematurity.",
